 and debuted as a member of the South Korean boy band Enhypen from the survival show I-Land in November 2020. Sunghoon is the 2016–2017 junior silver medalist and the 2015 novice gold medalist of Asian Figure Skating Trophy, and the 2015 novice gold medalist of Lombardia Trophy. He also won silver medals at the 2013 novice competition and the 2014 junior competition of South Korean Figure Skating Championships.","title":"Sunghoon (singer, born 2002)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunghoon_%28singer%2C_born_2002%29"}},"Q20972211":{"id":"Q20972211","name":"Wen Junhui","ko":"준","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Jun Hui Wen","Junhui","Jerry Wen","Jun","Moon Joon-hwi","Wen Jun Hui"],"birth":"1996-06-10","death":"","birthplace":"Shenzhen","nationality":["People's Republic of China"],"height":null,"occupations":["dancer","singer","actor","composer","choreographer"],"debut":"2015","agencies":[{"name":"Pledis Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q45282","start":"","end":""},{"name":"Hybe","korean":true,"id":"Q16161254","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q14524548","name":"Seventeen","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/jun.seventeen/","spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/38Gn0ZVC8TQwuaMxBK1yRV","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/564eb37b-a611-43cc-b128-9e0d4cc09026"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4c/Jun_Follow_240330_2.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jun_Follow_240330_2.jpg","author":"Seventeen","license":"CC BY 3.0"},"bio":{"text":"Wen Junhui, known professionally as Jun, is a Chinese singer, actor, and dancer working in South Korea and China. Managed by Pledis Entertainment, he is a member of the South Korean boy band Seventeen and its performance team. Before debuting as a member of Seventeen, Jun was a child actor who starred in multiple films including The Pye Dog (2007), The Legend Is Born: Ip Man (2010), and Chinese web drama Intouchable (2015). In 2023, he returned to acting with a lead role in iQIYI's Exclusive Fairytale. In 2025, he returned to films with a supporting role in The Shadow's Edge.","title":"Jun (Chinese entertainer)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jun_%28Chinese_entertainer%29"},"positions":["Sub vocalist","Lead dancer"],"mbti":"INFP","factSources":{"positions":{"name":"Namu Wiki (2021 dump)","license":"CC BY-NC-SA 2.0 KR","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.0/kr/","base":"https://namu.wiki/w/","url":"https://namu.wiki/w/%EC%A4%80%28%EC%84%B8%EB%B8%90%ED%8B%B4%29"},"mbti":{"name":"Namu Wiki (2021 dump)","license":"CC BY-NC-SA 2.0 KR","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.0/kr/","base":"https://namu.wiki/w/","url":"https://namu.wiki/w/%EC%A4%80%28%EC%84%B8%EB%B8%90%ED%8B%B4%29"}}},"Q21824947":{"id":"Q21824947","name":"Boo Seung-kwan","ko":"승관","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Seungkwan"],"birth":"1998-01-16","death":"","birthplace":"Busan","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"2015","agencies":[{"name":"Pledis Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q45282","start":"","end":""},{"name":"Hybe","korean":true,"id":"Q16161254","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q14524548","name":"Seventeen","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/pledis_boos/","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/e653c6c1-086c-4d7c-9117-b3480357d4f2"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Boo Seung-kwan, known mononymously as Seungkwan, is a South Korean singer. Managed by Pledis Entertainment, he is a member of the South Korean boy band Seventeen, its vocal team, and the subunit BSS alongside Hoshi and DK. Apart from his group's activities, Seungkwan is known as an entertainment figure for his active participation in Korean variety shows such as Unexpected Q, Prison Life of Fools, and The Devil's Plan. Seungkwan has also released a number of OSTs that have been commercially successful in South Korea.","title":"Seungkwan","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seungkwan"},"positions":["Main vocalist"],"mbti":"ENFP","factSources":{"positions":{"name":"Namu Wiki (2021 dump)","license":"CC BY-NC-SA 2.0 KR","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.0/kr/","base":"https://namu.wiki/w/","url":"https://namu.wiki/w/%EC%8A%B9%EA%B4%80"},"mbti":{"name":"Namu Wiki (2021 dump)","license":"CC BY-NC-SA 2.0 KR","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.0/kr/","base":"https://namu.wiki/w/","url":"https://namu.wiki/w/%EC%8A%B9%EA%B4%80"}}},"Q22974707":{"id":"Q22974707","name":"Lee Sun-bin","ko":"이선빈","birthName":"Lee Jin-kyung","birthNameEn":"Lee Jin-kyung","aliases":["Lee Jin-kyung"],"birth":"1994-01-07","death":"","birthplace":"Cheonan","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["actor","singer"],"debut":"2011","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q485691","name":"JQT","start":"2011","end":"2012"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/sunbin_eyesmag/","x":"https://x.com/ljk5151"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Lee Jin-kyung, known professionally as Lee Sun-bin (이선빈), is a South Korean actress and singer. She is a former member of the South Korean girl group JQT, and is known for starring in Squad 38 (2016), Work Later, Drink Now (2021–2023), and Boyhood (2023).","title":"Lee Sun-bin","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lee_Sun-bin"}},"Q23895155":{"id":"Q23895155","name":"Mint","ko":"민트","birthName":"Goonshipas Peonpaweevorakul","birthNameEn":"Goonshipas Peonpaweevorakul","aliases":["Goonshipas Peonpaweevorakul"],"birth":"1994-06-23","death":"","birthplace":"Bangkok","nationality":["Thailand"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q7808559","name":"Tiny-G","start":"2012","end":"2015"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/mintmswag/","x":"https://x.com/minttytinyg"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Goonshipas Peonpaweevorakul, better known by the nickname Mint, also known as Mintty, is a Thai singer based in South Korea. She was a member of the South Korean girl group Tiny-G.","title":"Mint (singer)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mint_%28singer%29"}},"Q253619":{"id":"Q253619","name":"Kim Hyo-yeon","ko":"효연","birthName":"김효연","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Kim Hyoyeon","Kim Hyo-yun","Kim Hyoyun","Kim Hyo Yun","Hyoyeon","Kim Hyo Yeon","HYO","DJ Hyo"],"birth":"1989-09-22","death":"","birthplace":"Incheon","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","rapper","dancer","model"],"debut":"2007","agencies":[{"name":"SM Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q483938","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q20153","name":"Girls' Generation","start":"2007","end":""},{"id":"Q56260975","name":"Girls' Generation-Oh!GG","start":"2018","end":""},{"id":"Q110310446","name":"Got the Beat","start":"2022","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/hyoyeon_x_x/","x":"https://x.com/Hyoyeon_djhyo","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCy09Uze1QeJPWycuOMPhjsw","tiktok":"https://www.tiktok.com/@dj_hyo","spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/0B3I6YgdnfXehUCpsO6oB8","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/f2911ba4-9eaf-4ae2-b7a2-0f27b7a955be"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/ca/20220323_%EC%86%8C%EB%85%80%EC%8B%9C%EB%8C%80_%ED%9A%A8%EC%97%B0.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:20220323_%EC%86%8C%EB%85%80%EC%8B%9C%EB%8C%80_%ED%9A%A8%EC%97%B0.jpg","author":"티비텐","license":"CC BY 3.0"},"bio":{"text":"Kim Hyo-yeon, known professionally as Hyoyeon or DJ Hyo, is a South Korean singer, dancer, rapper, and DJ. She debuted as a member of the girl group Girls' Generation in August 2007, which went on to become one of the best-selling artists in South Korea and one of the most widely known K-pop groups worldwide. She has since participated in other SM Entertainment projects, including Girls' Generation-Oh!GG and Got the Beat. Hyoyeon also released the solo singles \"Mystery\" (2016) and \"Wannabe\" (2017) prior to making her solo debut as Hyo with the single \"Sober\" in 2018.","title":"Hyoyeon","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hyoyeon"},"positions":["Sub vocalist","Main dancer"],"mbti":"ISTJ","factSources":{"positions":{"name":"Namu Wiki (2021 dump)","license":"CC BY-NC-SA 2.0 KR","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.0/kr/","base":"https://namu.wiki/w/","url":"https://namu.wiki/w/%ED%9A%A8%EC%97%B0"},"mbti":{"name":"Namu Wiki (2021 dump)","license":"CC BY-NC-SA 2.0 KR","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.0/kr/","base":"https://namu.wiki/w/","url":"https://namu.wiki/w/%ED%9A%A8%EC%97%B0"}}},"Q28661939":{"id":"Q28661939","name":"Meng Mei Qi","ko":"미기","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Mei Qi","Meng Meiqi","Mi Ki","Maeng Migi","Maeng Mi Gi","Maang Mei Kei","Mi Gi"],"birth":"1998-10-15","death":"","birthplace":"Luoyang","nationality":["People's Republic of China"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","dancer"],"debut":"2016","agencies":[{"name":"Starship Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q255363","start":"","end":""},{"name":"Yuehua Entertainment","korean":false,"id":"Q18390500","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q21964258","name":"WJSN","start":"2016","end":"2023"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/m.meiqi7/","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/0c447b22-cfb6-4ee5-8925-0f62e5a31cda"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Meng Meiqi is a Chinese singer and actress signed under Yuehua Entertainment. She began her career as a member of South Korean girl group WJSN in 2016 and went on hiatus from the group since early-2018 prior to leaving in 2023 due to the expiration of her contract. After finishing first in the Chinese edition of the survival show Produce 101, she became a member of the Chinese girl group Rocket Girls 101 in 2018.","title":"Meng Meiqi","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meng_Meiqi"}},"Q28969139":{"id":"Q28969139","name":"Heo Soo-yeon","ko":"허수연","birthName":"허수연","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Eunice","Heo Eunice"],"birth":"1991-09-02","death":"","birthplace":"Busan","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","actor"],"debut":"2015","agencies":[{"name":"MBK Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q429296","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q20733515","name":"DIA","start":"2015","end":"2022"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/e.heomer/"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ec/190320_%EB%8B%A4%EC%9D%B4%EC%95%84_%EC%9C%A0%EB%8B%88%EC%8A%A4.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:190320_%EB%8B%A4%EC%9D%B4%EC%95%84_%EC%9C%A0%EB%8B%88%EC%8A%A4.jpg","author":"NewsInStar","license":"CC BY 3.0"},"bio":{"text":"DIA is a South Korean girl group formed by MBK Entertainment. The group was composed of six members: Eunice, Jueun, Huihyeon, Yebin, Chaeyeon and Eunchae. DIA officially debuted on September 14, 2015, with their lead single \"Somehow\" from their debut album Do It Amazing. Seunghee left the group in April 2016 after her contract expired and she would pursue her acting career. In May 2018, Eunjin decided to leave the group for health reasons. Jenny later left the group in July 2019, similarly for health reasons like Eunjin. In January 2022, Somyi departed the group after deciding to terminate her exclusive contract.","title":"Eunice (singer)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eunice_%28singer%29"}},"Q4121203":{"id":"Q4121203","name":"Maya","ko":"마야","birthName":"김영숙","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Kim Young-sook","Kim Yeong-suk"],"birth":"1979-11-17","death":"","birthplace":"Chungju","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","film actor","actor","lyricist"],"debut":"2003","agencies":[],"groups":[],"links":{"x":"https://x.com/queenmayazzang","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/1c33b814-08f3-4d33-bcfe-494fd44e46f8"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Kim Young-sook, better known as Maya (마야) is a South Korean pop rock singer and actress. She debuted in 2003 with the album, Born To Do It, which included the hit single \"Azalea.\"","title":"Maya (singer)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maya_%28singer%29"}},"Q42302579":{"id":"Q42302579","name":"JinE","ko":"진이","birthName":"신혜진","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Shin Hye-jin"],"birth":"1995-01-22","death":"","birthplace":"Pohang","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"2015","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q19794854","name":"Oh My Girl","start":"2015","end":"2017"}],"links":{"musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/c898b34a-3931-4cc0-867e-e503691f6494"},"photo":null,"bio":null,"positions":["Sub vocalist"],"factSources":{"positions":{"name":"Namu Wiki (2021 dump)","license":"CC BY-NC-SA 2.0 KR","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.0/kr/","base":"https://namu.wiki/w/","url":"https://namu.wiki/w/%EC%8B%A0%ED%98%9C%EC%A7%84"}}},"Q483571":{"id":"Q483571","name":"Lee Seung-gi","ko":"이승기","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Lee Seung Gi"],"birth":"1987-01-13","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["actor","singer","master of ceremonies","television actor","recording artist"],"debut":"2004","agencies":[],"groups":[],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/leeseunggi.official/","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/aff0405a-9f74-48b0-b5fe-acfc138624f8"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8f/LeeSeunggi4.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LeeSeunggi4.jpg","author":"프로스펙스","license":"CC BY 3.0"},"bio":{"text":"Lee Seung-gi is a South Korean singer, actor, host, lyricist and entertainer. As one of the highest paid celebrities of South Korea and recipient of numerous awards and accolades, including a Golden Disc Award for music and Baeksang Arts Award for acting, Lee has been featured multiple times in Forbes Korea Power Celebrity 40 list since 2010, and recently ranked sixth in 2022. His success as a singer, actor and host has earned him the title of \"Triple Threat\" entertainer and has established him as a top Hallyu star. He has numerous hit songs as a singer such as \"Because You're My Woman\", \"Will You Marry Me\", \"Return\" and \"The Ordinary Man\".","title":"Lee Seung-gi","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lee_Seung-gi"},"mbti":"ENTJ","factSources":{"mbti":{"name":"Namu Wiki (2021 dump)","license":"CC BY-NC-SA 2.0 KR","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.0/kr/","base":"https://namu.wiki/w/","url":"https://namu.wiki/w/%EC%9D%B4%EC%8A%B9%EA%B8%B0"}}},"Q484403":{"id":"Q484403","name":"U-Nee","ko":"유니","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":[],"birth":"1981-05-03","death":"2007-01-21","birthplace":"Goyang","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","film actor","actor"],"debut":"1996","agencies":[],"groups":[],"links":{"musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/41cb44ba-1e4d-4b1a-a9d2-99847c58ef06"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Heo Yun (Korean: 허윤; born Lee Hye-ryeon (이혜련), May 3, 1981 – January 21, 2007), best known professionally as U;Nee (유니), was a South Korean singer, rapper, dancer and actress. She made her debut as a singer with her first album U;Nee Code (2003). U;Nee died by suicide on January 21, 2007, at age 25.","title":"U;Nee","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U%3BNee"}},"Q489459":{"id":"Q489459","name":"Zhou Mi","ko":"조미","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":[],"birth":"1986-04-19","death":"","birthplace":"Wuhan","nationality":["People's Republic of China"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","songwriter","actor","television actor","recording artist"],"debut":"2008","agencies":[{"name":"SM Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q483938","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q706116","name":"Super Junior-M","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/zhouzhoumi419/","x":"https://x.com/zhoumi_419","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/b3806a2d-76e6-4a71-9eed-4e963e2134e4"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Zhou Mi is a Chinese singer active in South Korea and China signed under SM and co-managed with Baymon for his China-based activities. He debuted in 2008 as an exclusive member of the Super Junior's Chinese sub-group Super Junior-M, and later participated in SM Entertainment's project group SM the Ballad. Aside from group activities, he also participates in various television variety shows, radio shows, and dramas. He released his first solo EP entitled Rewind in 2014. In 2016, SM established its own management group for his activities in China, Zhoumi Studio (周觅工作室).","title":"Zhou Mi","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zhou_Mi"},"positions":["Main vocalist","Sub rapper"],"factSources":{"positions":{"name":"Namu Wiki (2021 dump)","license":"CC BY-NC-SA 2.0 KR","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.0/kr/","base":"https://namu.wiki/w/","url":"https://namu.wiki/w/%EC%A1%B0%EB%AF%B8%28%EC%8A%88%ED%8D%BC%EC%A3%BC%EB%8B%88%EC%96%B4-M%29"}}},"Q493619":{"id":"Q493619","name":"Jung Yoon-hak","ko":"윤학","birthName":"정윤학","birthNameEn":"","aliases":[],"birth":"1984-12-02","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"2007","agencies":[{"name":"Universal Music Group","korean":false,"id":"Q38903","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/unagi1202/","x":"https://x.com/chyh1202","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/80df6c3c-11b0-461e-9760-7094fd74d3b1"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Jung Yoon-hak is a South Korean actor, model and singer. He is the leader of Supernova, and member of its sub-unit Double Ace, along with fellow vocalist SungJe. He is known for his lead roles in My Unfortunate Boyfriend, Bouncer and Ichijiku no Mori.","title":"Jung Yoon-hak","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jung_Yoon-hak"}},"Q57599411":{"id":"Q57599411","name":"Ray","ko":"레이 (1994년)","birthName":"김현일","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Kim Hyun-il"],"birth":"1994-04-19","death":"","birthplace":"Pohang","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q491944","name":"C-Clown","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/hyeon__il/"},"photo":null,"bio":null},"Q63378931":{"id":"Q63378931","name":"Jun Eun-mi","ko":"전은미 (1984년)","birthName":"전은미","birthNameEn":"","aliases":[],"birth":"1984-10-16","death":"","birthplace":"","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["actor","singer","stage actor"],"debut":"","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q490873","name":"Jewelry","start":"","end":""}],"links":{},"photo":null,"bio":null},"Q65058867":{"id":"Q65058867","name":"Song Hyeong-jun","ko":"송형준","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Song Hyeongjun","Hyeongjun","Song Hyeong Jun"],"birth":"2002-11-30","death":"","birthplace":"Tongyeong","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","dancer"],"debut":"2019","agencies":[{"name":"Starship Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q255363","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q65665588","name":"X1","start":"2019","end":""},{"id":"Q90628571","name":"Cravity","start":"2020","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/x1official101/"},"photo":null,"bio":null,"positions":["Vocalist"],"factSources":{"positions":{"name":"Namu Wiki (2021 dump)","license":"CC BY-NC-SA 2.0 KR","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.0/kr/","base":"https://namu.wiki/w/","url":"https://namu.wiki/w/%ED%98%95%EC%A4%80"}}},"Q65762547":{"id":"Q65762547","name":"Park Sung-jin","ko":"성진","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Sungjin"],"birth":"1993-01-16","death":"","birthplace":"Busan","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","guitarist"],"debut":"2015","agencies":[{"name":"JYP Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q483238","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q20898046","name":"Day6","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/day6kilogram/","x":"https://x.com/DAY6__SUNGJIN"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Park Sung-jin, known mononymously as Sungjin, is a South Korean musician, singer, songwriter, and guitarist. He is best known as the leader, guitarist and vocalist of South Korean pop rock band Day6.","title":"Sungjin","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sungjin"}},"Q7694067":{"id":"Q7694067","name":"Teddy Park","ko":"테디","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Park Hong-joon","Teddy","TEDDY","Park Hong Jun","Ted Hong Jun Park","Te Di","Park Hong-jun"],"birth":"1978-09-14","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["rapper","singer","songwriter","record producer","musician"],"debut":"1998","agencies":[{"name":"YG Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q50595","start":"","end":""},{"name":"The Black Label","korean":true,"id":"Q24866458","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q485884","name":"1TYM","start":"1998","end":"2006"}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/teddypark__/","x":"https://x.com/_teddypark","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/fd65c60b-2aaa-4537-85c8-18b07c9a12e7"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Teddy Park is a Korean-American rapper, songwriter, and record producer based in South Korea. He first gained attention as a member of the hip hop group 1TYM and gained prominence as a producer for YG Entertainment and his own entertainment company The Black Label. Park has received several accolades including an Academy Award, a Grammy Award, and a Golden Globe Award. Forbes magazine describes him as the \"K-pop/rap star turned prolific music producer who has helped shape and aid South Korean music's global crossover\". Born in Seoul, South Korea, Park moved to the United States with his family as a young child.","title":"Teddy Park","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teddy_Park"},"positions":["Leader","Main rapper","Producer"],"factSources":{"positions":{"name":"Namu Wiki (2021 dump)","license":"CC BY-NC-SA 2.0 KR","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.0/kr/","base":"https://namu.wiki/w/","url":"https://namu.wiki/w/%ED%85%8C%EB%94%94%28%EC%9B%90%ED%83%80%EC%9E%84%29"}}},"Q8058611":{"id":"Q8058611","name":"Yoo Young-jae","ko":"유영재","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Youngjae"],"birth":"1994-01-24","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","actor"],"debut":"2012","agencies":[{"name":"TS Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q491998","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q483234","name":"B.A.P","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/yjaybaby/","x":"https://x.com/BAP_Youngjae","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/fc4a7e9b-392e-416b-9471-142740ef471b"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Yoo Young-jae, also known mononymously as Youngjae, is a South Korean singer and actor. He debuted as an idol in the six-member group B.A.P under TS Entertainment, where he served as the main vocalist from 2012 to its dissolution in 2019. He released his debut mini-album Fancy in April 2019.","title":"Yoo Young-jae","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yoo_Young-jae"},"positions":["Lead vocalist"],"factSources":{"positions":{"name":"Namu Wiki (2021 dump)","license":"CC BY-NC-SA 2.0 KR","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.0/kr/","base":"https://namu.wiki/w/","url":"https://namu.wiki/w/%EC%9C%A0%EC%98%81%EC%9E%AC"}}}}}